Here are three educational documents, listed in ascending order of complexity.

# ((What Is Lojban?, The Book|What Is Lojban?)), an introductory book covering a wide range of basic information on the Lojban language.
#  Robin Turner and Nick Nicholas's [http://ptolemy.tlg.uci.edu/~opoudjis/lojbanbrochure/lessons/book1.html|Lojban For Beginners] lessons.
#  The [http://www.lojban.org/jbovlaste/|jbovlaste dictionary interface,] a way to browse and enter Lojban word definitions.
    
There is a Lojban-to-English translator at [http://www.lojban.org/jboski/].

You could also try ((Parallel 2)), a program for ((implicit learning)) of Lojban (and other languages).

Finally, you can [http://www.lojban.org/lsg2/|join the Lojban beginner's e-mail list].


There is also a [http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-download_wiki_attachment.php?attId=89|PDF of the first 19 pages of the Level 0 booklet.]